<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<quiz>
<question type="stack">
<name>
<text>Equation line given two points ask find equation</text>
</name>
<questiontext format="html">
<text><![CDATA[<p>A line passes through the points \(A({@xa@}, {@ya@})\) and \(B({@xb@}, {@yb@})\).</p>
<p>Find the equation of the line, written in the form \(y=mx+c\).</p>
<p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt_ans1]]</p>]]></text>
</questiontext>
<questionvariables>
<text>c: rand_with_prohib(-9, 9, [0]);
q: rand([2,3,4,5]);
plist: if q=2 then [1,3,5,7,9] elseif q=3 then [1,2,4,5,7,8] elseif q=4 then [1,3,5,7,9] else [1,2,3,4,6,7,8,9];
sg: rand([-1,1]);
p: sg*rand(plist);
a: rand(2)+1;
b: rand(2)+1;
m: p/q;
xa: -q*a;
xb: q*b;
ya: m*xa+c;
yb: m*xb+c;
ta1: y = m*x+c;
rhsT: m*x+c;</text>
</questionvariables>
<generalfeedback format="html">
<text><![CDATA[<p>The gradient is \(m=\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}=\frac{{@yb@}-({@ya@})}{{@xb@}-({@xa@})}={@m@}\).</p>
<p>Substitute \(A({@xa@},{@ya@})\) into \(y=mx+c\): \({@ya@}={@m@}\cdot({@xa@})+c\), so \(c={@c@}\).</p>
<p>The line is \({@ta1@}\).</p>]]></text>
</generalfeedback>
<specificfeedback format="html">
  <text></text>
</specificfeedback>
<questionnote format="moodle_auto_format">
<text>\(m={@m@}, c={@c@}, a={@a@}, b={@b@}\)</text>
</questionnote>
<penalty>0</penalty>
<input>
<name>ans1</name>
<type>algebraic</type>
<tans>ta1</tans>
<syntaxhint>y=...</syntaxhint>
<insertstars>1</insertstars>
<boxsize>15</boxsize>
<strictsyntax>1</strictsyntax>
<syntaxattribute>0</syntaxattribute>
<forbidwords></forbidwords>
<allowwords></allowwords>
<forbidfloat>1</forbidfloat>
<requirelowestterms>0</requirelowestterms>
<checkanswertype>0</checkanswertype>
<mustverify>1</mustverify>
<showvalidation>1</showvalidation>
<options></options>
</input>
<prt>
  <name>prt_ans1</name>
  <value>1</value>
  <autosimplify>1</autosimplify>
  <feedbackstyle>1</feedbackstyle>
  <feedbackvariables>
    <text>iseq: is(equationp(ans1));
yleft: is(iseq and lhs(ans1)=y);
rt: if yleft then rhs(ans1) else 0;
ok: is(yleft and algebraic_equivalence(rt, rhsT));
inv: is(yleft and algebraic_equivalence(rt, (q/p)*x+c));
neg: is(yleft and algebraic_equivalence(rt, -m*x+c));
swp: is(yleft and algebraic_equivalence(rt, c*x+p/q));</text>
  </feedbackvariables>
  <node>
    <name>0</name>
    <description>Is it an equation?</description>
    <answertest>AlgEquiv</answertest>
    <sans>iseq</sans>
    <tans>true</tans>
    <truenextnode>1</truenextnode>
    <quiet>0</quiet>
